## Sign in with Apple + Supabase (March 2026)

**What we learned**

- **Dashboard fields:** Supabase **Authentication → Providers → Apple** may show only **Client IDs** (one field) and **Secret Key (for OAuth)** — not separate Team ID / Key ID / private key boxes. The **Secret Key** is the Apple **client secret** (JWT) built from Team ID, Key ID, and the `.p8` signing key; Apple requires rotating that secret about **every 6 months** (Supabase shows an orange warning). Use Supabase’s doc helper or their generator; **Safari can break** the in-browser generator — prefer Chrome/Firefox.

- **Client IDs is a comma-separated allow list:** The help text is explicit: native bundle IDs **and/or** Services IDs. You must list **every** identity Apple may put in the ID token **`aud` (audience)** claim:
  - **Services ID** (e.g. `com.sleepfactor.app.login`) — used for web/OAuth and registered with Apple’s **Website URLs** pointing at `https://<project-ref>.supabase.co` and redirect `https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback`.
  - **All iOS app bundle IDs** that use native Sign in with Apple — for SleepFactor: **`com.sleepfactor.app`** (production) and **`com.sleepfactor.app.dev`** (EAS development / dev client). Omitting the dev bundle ID causes: **`Unacceptable audience in id_token: [com.sleepfactor.app.dev]`** when testing a dev build.

- **Example one-line value:** `com.sleepfactor.app.login,com.sleepfactor.app,com.sleepfactor.app.dev` (order does not matter; commas, no duplicate entries).

- **Apple Developer (minimal checklist):** App ID(s) → **Sign in with Apple** capability on. **Services ID** → Sign in with Apple **Configure** → Primary App ID = main app (`com.sleepfactor.app`) → domain = `<project-ref>.supabase.co`, return URL = Supabase callback above. **Key** with Sign in with Apple → download `.p8` once; use Key ID + Team ID when generating the OAuth secret for Supabase.

- **After fixing Client IDs only:** Changing Supabase provider settings does **not** require a new iOS build — retry sign-in immediately. New builds are still needed when changing native entitlements, bundle ID, or app config plugins.

- **Platform note:** Native Sign in with Apple is **iOS-only** in practice for this stack; Android uses other auth paths. Docs: `docs/NATIVE_LOGIN_SETUP.txt`, Supabase [Login with Apple](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/social-login/auth-apple).

